AirliftFFI core — wholesale transplant from AirCard-iOS
--------------------------------------------------------
The entire device write path of this app (loopback tunnel connection,
RemotePairing session, AFC staging, AirTraffic sync, PosterBoard
injection, refresh writes, respring) is the AirliftFFI Rust core of
the AirCard-iOS project, vendored verbatim into `rust-core/`:

  Project:  AirCard-iOS
  Author:   Johnny Franks (Mak5er)
  Source:   https://github.com/Mak5er/AirCard-iOS
  Version:  v1.3.2, upstream commit
            40640c4d827aeab8d798285b57d24fcf6be070d0
  Path:     rust-core/ (crate `airlift_ffi`: src/, include/, vendor/)
  License:  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Johnny Franks

See rust-core/VENDORED.md for the vendoring record. The vendored
sources are unmodified; only the build wiring differs (the app links
the produced static library directly instead of packaging an
xcframework).

The app-side Grappa helper `Sources/App/GrappaHelper.h` /
`GrappaHelper.m` is likewise the upstream file, copied verbatim from
the same commit: the core resolves its `ALGetGrappaToken` symbol at
runtime (dlsym) and the helper tries a framework host session first,
then verifies each candidate from its built-in authentic token table
(kAuthenticGrappaTokens, also from AirCard-iOS) against a device
session before adopting one.

App layer — wholesale transplant from AirCard-iOS
---------------------------------------------------
The entire app layer in `Sources/App/` is the upstream AirCard-iOS
app (the `ios-app/` directory of the same project, same version
v1.3.2, same upstream commit 40640c4d827aeab8d798285b57d24fcf6be070d0),
copied verbatim: all Swift sources, `Info.plist`, and the Grappa
helper. Views, copy, pairing host name, pairing-file locations,
logs and flows are unchanged from upstream. The only differences
from the upstream app are identity and build wiring:

  * Bundle identifier is com.coco.cocowall (upstream:
    com.mak5er.aircard), and `CFBundleDisplayName` is "CocoWall";
    these are the only two edits inside the copied files.
  * The app icon is CocoWall's own (upstream's icon set is not
    carried over; `Sources/App/icon-1024.b64` decodes to the single
    1024px icon at build time).
  * The project is generated from this repository's `project.yml`:
    sources live under `Sources/App/` instead of upstream's
    `ios-app/`, the vendored core is linked as a static library
    instead of an xcframework, and the deployment target is
    iOS 17.0 (upstream: 18.0).
  * Upstream's unit tests (`tests/` in the upstream repository)
    are not carried over; nothing in the app depends on them.

Like upstream, the app ships no packet-tunnel extension: the
loopback tunnel is provided by an external VPN app (LocalDevVPN).
CocoWall's former in-house app layer and its bundled tunnel
extension target were removed in this transplant.

